Carafe: a thread's call-return stack takes 512 KB instead of 4 MB.
The stack only predicts where a guest RET goes; when it runs over, the guard page resets it. Every thread of a
32-bit game took 4 MB of the game's own 4 GB for it, committed, and with some 80 threads the address space ran
out and threads could no longer start or end (the threads probe's churn phase). 512 KB still holds 32768
nested calls.
MIT, as the file it changes.

--- a/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h
+++ b/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h
@@ -109,7 +109,7 @@
   ///< Data pointer for exclusive use by the frontend
   void* FrontendPtr;
 
-  static constexpr size_t CALLRET_STACK_SIZE {0x400000};
+  static constexpr size_t CALLRET_STACK_SIZE {0x80000};
 
   // The low address of the call-ret stack allocation (not including guard pages)
   void* CallRetStackBase {};
